symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6555,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"Callers: `binding_jira_key_map` (once per `search_state`) and `_resolve_via_binding_store` (once per Jira-key-shaped id in `resolve_ticket_id`).\"","grep for binding_jira_key_map surfaces three call sites: src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:567, src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:74, plus the definition in src/rebar/_ids.py:104","src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:74 `if resolved in binding_jira_key_map(str(tracker)):` inside _enforce_promote_only (called from composer_edit.py:306)"],"finding":"The caller inventory for binding_jira_key_map is incomplete: the plan names only the per-search_state caller (reads.py:567) but omits a third, out-of-module caller, _enforce_promote_only in src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:74, which calls binding_jira_key_map(str(tracker)) during an EDIT command to decide whether a ticket is already bound.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6c7e357a67c57d0e","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem — \"Callers: `binding_jira_key_map` (once per `search_state`) and `_resolve_via_binding_store` ...\"","norm_id":"ne065c8dd99221b24","priority":0.2445,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:74 (_enforce_promote_only): the promote-only guard reads binding_jira_key_map mid-EDIT; under the new per-process cache its freshness token (os.stat mtime_ns/size) now governs whether this correctness check sees a binding written earlier in the same long-lived process, a behavioral surface the plan never considers.","Plan's read-only/shared-map reasoning is scoped to 'both in-module callers' and silently excludes this out-of-module caller, so no one has reasoned about cache-staleness correctness for the bind-promote guard."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Problem section's caller list, add the composer_edit._enforce_promote_only caller of binding_jira_key_map, and extend approach C's staleness analysis to confirm the os.stat freshness token correctly re-reads a binding written earlier in the same process before this promote-only guard runs.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the cache's concurrency assumption (single-threaded callers, or that the store is idempotent and consumers treat the map read-only so a populate race is benign), matching the _TOML_CACHE/_file_token precedent.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.818,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a long-lived process (MCP server) re-parses the unchanged file on every call' names the concurrent consumer","Plan: 'Memoize the parsed reverse map in a module-level dict keyed by bindings path' — shared mutable state with no stated lock","Plan cites precedent _TOML_CACHE and _file_token which are presumably equally unlocked, suggesting an accepted single-threaded-or-idempotent pattern"],"finding":"The per-process cache is module-level mutable shared state consumed in a long-lived MCP server, but the plan never states its concurrency model. The read path is check-then-act (os.stat compare -> maybe open+parse -> store into the module dict); if the MCP server services requests on multiple threads, two threads can race to populate/replace the entry. The result is benign/idempotent (both compute the same reverse map and consumers treat it read-only), and the plan cites _TOML_CACHE/_file_token as the same unlocked pattern, so this is a documentation/assurance gap rather than a correctness bug — but the lifecycle writeup should say so explicitly.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3bdc6ff7a1def0db","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'C — per-process cache' / 'A call whose current os.stat token matches the stored one returns the cached map'","norm_id":"n5f70308341231610","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["MCP server handling concurrent resolve_ticket_id / search_state requests re-parses bindings.json redundantly under a race, or stores a map twice; outcome is correct but the plan has not confirmed read/write access to the shared dict is safe"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to the C paragraph: the cache store is idempotent (same path -> same reverse map), consumers never mutate it, so a concurrent populate under the MCP server is benign and no lock is required — identical to the existing _TOML_CACHE/_file_token pattern.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"n